{"id":"word:hebrew:H567","type":"word","title":"אֱמֹרִי","subtitle":"H567 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"an Emorite , one of the Canaanitish tribes","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֱמֹרִי (H567) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 87 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֱמֹרִי (ʼĔmôrîy) means an Emorite , one of the Canaanitish tribes First listed occurrence: 1Chr 1 14."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֱמֹרִי","transliteration":"ʼĔmôrîy","pronunciation":"em-o-ree'","strong":"H567","lemmaId":"hebrew:H567","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הָ/אֱמֹרִ֔י","הָ/אֱמֹרִ֖י","הָֽ/אֱמֹרִ֔י","הָ֣/אֱמֹרִ֔י","הָ/אֱמֹרִֽי"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ngmsa",71],["HC/Td/Ngmsa",13],["HNgmsa",2],["HRd/Ngmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"an Emorite , one of the Canaanitish tribes","usage":"Amorite.","full":"H567. Emori אֱמֹרִי proper name, masculine collective (construed as plural Deut 3:9 5 t.) Amorites (perhaps = mountain-dwellers , compare Num 13:29 ; Deut 1:7 , 19 f. etc. & Di Gen 10:16 and elsewhere) **meaning mountain-dwellers very dubious; on ׳א = Egyptian 'A-ma-ra see WMM As.u.Eur.229ff. , = Tel Amarna and Assyrian Amurru , see Wkl TelAm. 36* Jastr EB CANAAN, § 10 Say Hast.DB AMORITES and others; compare also GFM Judg 4:5 Dr Dt l.7 Gray Num 13:29 . — always with article, except 21:29 ; Ezek 16:45 . 1 called son of Canaan Gen 10:16 (J) 1Chr 1:14 = 2 a chief people dispossessed by Hebrews ; (a) living east of Jordan Num 21:13 (twice in verse); 21:25 9 t. Numbers + Josh 24:8 (all E), compare 2:10 ; 9:10 (JE) Deut 1:4 ; 3:2 , 9 7 t. D; also Judg 10:8 , 11 ; 11:19 , 21 , 23 (twice in verse); 1Kin 4:19 ; Psa 135:11 ; 136:19 (Sihon their king Num 21:1 +; Sihon & Og Deut 3:8 + ); (b) living west of Jordan Josh 10:5-6 , 24:12 , 15 , 18 (all E), compare 7:7 (JE); 5:1 ; 10:12 (both D; compare also 13:4 , q. strike out Di) Judg 1:34-35 , 36 ; 6:10 ; 1Kin 21:26 ; 2Kin 21:11 compare 1Sam 21:2 ; (c) living in south Deut 1:7 , 19 , 20 , 27 , 44 ; compare Gen 14:7 (west of Dead Sea); (d) in General = ancient inhabitants of Canaan 15:16 (J or R) 48:22 (E) Amos 2:9-10 , (e) named in list of Canaanitish peoples, to be dispossessed by Israel Exod 3:8 , 17 ; 13:5 ; 33:2 ; 34:11 ; Josh 3:10 ; 9:1 (all J); Deut 7:1 ; 20:17 ; Josh 11:3 ; 12:8 (all D); Exod 23:23 ; Num 13:29 ; Josh 24:11 (all E); Judg 3:5 ; 1Kin 9:20 ; 2Chr 8:7 ; Ezra 9:1 ; Neh 9:8 ; compare Ezek 16:3 , 45 ; (on these lists compare Bu Urgesch 344 ff. & We JBTh xxi. 602 .) 3. adjective, of a people singular Gen 14:13 Deut 2:24 .","rootNote":"probably a patronymic from an unused name derived from 559 in the sense of publicity , i.e. prominence; thus, a mountaineer ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 1 14","keyReferences":["1Chr 1 14","1Kgs 4 19","1Kgs 9 20","1Kgs 21 26","1Sam 7 14","2Chr 8 7","2Kgs 21 11","2Sam 21 2"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":87,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 1 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ֣/אֱמֹרִ֔י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 4 19","book":"1Kgs","chapter":4,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֱמֹרִ֗י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 9 20","book":"1Kgs","chapter":9,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֱמֹרִ֜י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 21 26","book":"1Kgs","chapter":21,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֱמֹרִ֔י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 7 14","book":"1Sam","chapter":7,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֱמֹרִֽי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ngmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 8 7","book":"2Chr","chapter":8,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הָ/אֱמֹרִ֤י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ngmsa"},{"ref